  "unit": "u06-bazaar",
  "title": "Haggling",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Bargaining is normal in a bazaar, but not in fixed-price shops. Three chunks get you far:\n\n- **দাম একটু কম রাখেন।** — 'Lower the price a little, please.' (lit. 'keep the price a little less')\n- **এত দাম কেন?** — 'Why so expensive?'\n- **শেষ দাম কত?** — 'What's your final price?'\n\n**রাখেন** (*rakhen*) is the polite command of 'keep'; with a price it means 'make it…': **দুইশ টাকা রাখেন**. (Standard/Kolkata: **রাখুন**.) **কম** 'less' vs **বেশি** 'more'; **সস্তা** 'cheap' vs **দামি** 'expensive' (from দাম).\n\nTo refuse, **লাগবে না** ('I don't need it') is polite and final. To agree: **ঠিক আছে** 'OK'. Adjectives negate with **না**: **ভালো না** 'not good'.\n\n*Etiquette:* smile, name a fair price, and once the vendor says ঠিক আছে you've agreed. Haggle most over clothes and rickshaw fares; per-kilo vegetable prices are close to fixed.",
